ZLSpectrumEqualizer for WebCLAP (ports/zl-spectrum-equalizer): its window in the style of openDAW's device panels
(docs/device-panel-design.md), applied after zl-spectrum-equalizer-webclap.patch: state_definitions.hpp, the editor's
default colours; ui_state.hpp, the default band and curve colours; interface_definitons.cpp, flat surfaces
(the shadow helpers draw no shadows, a recessed area is a flat darker screen);
two_value_rotary_slider.hpp, openDAW's knob (a faint track around a dark cap, the value as an arc in the label
cream, no pointer); compact_linear_slider.hpp, a value as a thin cream bar; PluginEditor.cpp,
openDAW's font, Rubik Medium.

